	 6.5	 Conservation of Momentum
From Newton’s second law, you know that to accelerate an object, a net force 
must be applied to it. This chapter states much the same thing, but in different Momentum is conserved for all 

collisions, both elastic and inelastic 
language. If you wish to change the momentum of an object, exert an impulse (whenever external forces don’t 
