for example, disturbing Jupiter’s otherwise smooth path, and Jupiter does the same 
to Saturn. Both planets “wobble” in their orbits. The interplanetary forces that 
cause this wobbling are called perturbations.

By the 1840s, studies of the most recently discovered planet at the time, Uranus, 
