protons. Protons have a positive electric charge that repels other positive charges 
but attracts negative charges. So like kinds of electric charges repel one another, 
and unlike charges attract one another. It is the positive protons in the nucleus that 
attract a surrounding cloud of negatively charged electrons to constitute an atom. 
(The strong nuclear force, which binds the protons to neutrons and to each other 
within the nucleus, is described in Chapter 33.)

