relatively low pressure that exerts the lifting force against the piston is about the 
same as the air pressure in automobile tires.

Hydraulics is employed by modern devices ranging from very small to enor-
mous. Note the hydraulic pistons in almost all construction machines where heavy 
loads are involved. The many applications of Pascal’s principle have truly changed 
the landscape of our world.

