	 18.8	 Entropy
Energy tends to disperse: Hot air in a hot oven disperses when the oven door 
is  opened. Energy tends to degrade: Energy locked in the chemical bonds 
of wood degrades when the wood is burned. Entropy is the term we use to 
describe the natural dispersing or degrading of energy. Entropy can be meas-
ured by the amount of disorder in a system.11 More entropy means more dispersal 
or more degradation of energy. Since energy tends to disperse and degrade with 
time, the total amount of entropy in any system tends to increase with time. 
Whenever a physical system is allowed to distribute its energy freely, it always F i g u r e  1 8 .1 8
does so in a manner such that entropy increases while the energy of the system Entropy.
