We call the reflection of sound an echo. The fraction of energy carried by the re-
flected sound wave can be large if the surface is rigid and smooth, and small if the 
surface is soft and irregular. Sound energy that is not carried by the reflected sound 
wave is carried by the “transmitted” (absorbed) wave.

