21.1 Noise and Music
Most of the sounds we hear are noises. The impact of a falling object, the slam-
ming of a door, the roaring of a motorcycle, and most of the sounds from traffic in 
city streets are noises. Noise corresponds to an irregular vibration of the eardrum 
produced by some irregular vibration in our surroundings, a jumble of wavelengths 
and amplitudes. White noise is a mixture of a variety of frequencies of sound, just 
as white light is a mixture of all the frequencies of light. We describe the sound of 
the surf, rustling leaves, or bubbling water in a brook as white noise.

Music is the art of sound and has a different character. Musical sounds have pe-
