electrons will spread to all parts of its surface because the transferred electrons 
repel one another. If it is a poor conductor, it may be necessary to touch the rod 
at several places on the object in order to get a more or less uniform distribution 
of charge.

Charging by Induction
If you bring a charged object near a conducting surface, electrons are made to 
move in the surface material, even without physical contact. Consider the two 
insulated metal spheres, A and B, in Figure 22.7. In part (a), the spheres touch 
