enough to balance the influence of the rod: The charge is redistributed. In parts 
(c) and (d), if the spheres are separated while the rod is still present, each will be 
equally and oppositely charged. This is charging by induction. The charged 
rod has never touched the spheres, and the rod retains the same charge it had 
initially.

