	 24.2	 Magnetic Poles
The forces that magnets exert on one another are similar to electrical forces be-
cause both can attract and repel without touching, depending on which ends of 
the magnets are held near one another. Also like electrical forces, the strength of 
their interaction depends on the separation distance between the two magnets. 
Whereas electric charge is responsible for electrical forces, regions called magnetic 
poles give rise to magnetic forces.

