rock. The process is similar for sedimentary rocks, where magnetic domains 
in grains of iron that settle in sediments tend to align themselves with Earth’s 
magnetic field and become locked into the rock that forms. The slight magnet-
ism that results can be measured with sensitive instruments. As samples of rock 
are tested from different strata formed throughout geologic time, the magnetic 
field of Earth for different periods can be charted. This evidence shows that 
there have been times when the magnetic field of Earth has diminished to zero, 
