The universe is a shooting gallery of charged particles. They are called cosmic 
rays and consist of protons, alpha particles, and other atomic nuclei stripped 
of electrons, as well as high-energy electrons. The protons may be remnants of 
the Big Bang; the heavier nuclei probably boiled off from exploding stars. In 
any event, they travel through space at fantastic speeds and make up the cosmic 

