Every artist knows that if you mix red, green, and blue paint, the result will 
not be white but a muddy dark brown. Red and green paint certainly do not 
combine to form yellow, as is the rule for mixing colored lights. Mixing pig-
ments in paints and dyes is entirely different from mixing lights. Pigments are 
tiny particles that absorb specific colors. For example, pigments that produce 



