tained uranium. The next day he discovered to his surprise that the photographic 
plate had been darkened, apparently by spontaneous radiation from the uranium. 
He went on to show that this new radiation could ionize air and differed from X-
rays in that it could be deflected by electric and magnetic fields.  

It was soon discovered that similar rays are emitted by other elements, such as 
