Any number of experiments can be devised to detect accelerated motion, but 

none can be devised, according to Einstein, to detect a state of uniform motion. 
Therefore, absolute motion has no meaning. It would be very peculiar if the laws 
of mechanics varied for observers moving at different speeds. It would mean, 
for example, that a pool player on a smoothly moving ocean liner would have to 
adjust her style of play to the speed of the ship, or even to the season as Earth 
